Verse 1:
[Db]Once our blessed Christ of beauty [Ab]Was veiled off from human [Db]view;
[Db]But through suffering, death and sorrow [Ebm7]He has rent the [Ab7]veil in [Db]two.
[Gb]O behold the Man of [Db]Sorrows, [Gb]O be[Eb7]hold Him in plain [Ab7]view;
[Db]Lo! He [Eb7]is the [Db]mighty [Gb]Conqueror, [Db]Since He [Ab]rent the veil in [Db]two.
[Gb]Lo! He is the mighty [Db]Conqueror, [Ab]Since He [Ab7]rent the veil in [Db]two.

